\itemize{
\item \strong{High-level (recommended)} — ggplot2 Geoms with standard
aesthetics: \code{\link[=geom_odum_source]{geom_odum_source()}}, \code{\link[=geom_odum_producer]{geom_odum_producer()}},
\code{\link[=geom_odum_consumer]{geom_odum_consumer()}}, \code{\link[=geom_odum_storage]{geom_odum_storage()}},
\code{\link[=geom_odum_interaction]{geom_odum_interaction()}}, \code{\link[=geom_odum_heat_sink]{geom_odum_heat_sink()}},
\code{\link[=geom_odum_money]{geom_odum_money()}}. Vectorised over data rows; composable in a
\code{ggplot()} pipeline like any other ggplot2 layer.
\item \strong{Low-level} — vertex-tibble helpers that return \verb{(x, y, id)}
coordinates suitable for \code{geom_polygon()}: \code{\link[=odum_circle]{odum_circle()}},
\code{\link[=odum_producer]{odum_producer()}}, \code{\link[=odum_consumer]{odum_consumer()}}, \code{\link[=odum_storage]{odum_storage()}},
\code{\link[=odum_interaction]{odum_interaction()}}, \code{\link[=odum_heat_sink]{odum_heat_sink()}}, \code{\link[=odum_money]{odum_money()}}.
Use these when you want to hand-compose polygons, animate with
\code{gganimate}, or overlay on non-ggplot renderers.
